The language filter is now in place and working. Here's what was implemented:

1. **A prominent language filter selector** (`🌐 Filter by language:`) has been added right below the page header ("Just Chatting & IRL") and above the stream grid. It has a dark background with purple accent text to match Twitch's theme.

2. **It auto-detects available languages** from the visible stream cards by looking at their language tags (e.g., `[data-a-target="English"]`). Only actual language tags are included — non-language tags like "TogetherForGood" or "ASMR" are filtered out using a comprehensive known-languages dictionary.

3. **When you select a language**, all streams that don't have that language tag are hidden (`display: none`). Selecting "All languages" restores the full list.

4. **The filter is persistent** — it will be recreated whenever the page loads or the content refreshes, and it always rebuilds from scratch to pick up any newly loaded streams' languages.

